  ],
  "details": "<p>According to the \"Iraq Significant Sites\" register, Tell Harmal (the ancient:\u00a0<em>Shaduppum</em>) is located in Iraq\u2019s Baghdad Governorate, on the outskirts of southern Baghdad. This site is a \u201csmall, heavily fortified city in what is now a suburb of Baghdad, where an early law code was discovered.\u201d The site dates to the middle of the third millennium to the second millennium BCE.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
